  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh - Netherlands Seed Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SeedNL, in collaboration with Wageningen University &amp; Research, Naktuinbouw, the Dutch Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, Food Security and Nature, and Innovision, conducted an in-depth assessment of the seed sector in Bangladesh during 2023. This report focused on the seed systems for potatoes, vegetables and flowers, identifying critical challenges and opportunities for developing a robust seed sector in Bangladesh.Building on these findings, a formal partnership between the Netherlands and Bangladesh will be entered, the Bangladesh-Netherlands Seed Partnership. This Partnership will foster public-private collaboration, support information exchange, and address sector challenges, ultimately creating a conducive environment for investment in the seed sector.This project aims to create a comprehensive platform that brings together key stakeholders to drive a strategic and sustainable transformation of Bangladesh&apos;s seed sector, including a contribution to a better enabling environment for the Bangladesh&#x2019;s seed sector. The first concrete activity is the establishment of a seed platform with a local seed secretariat and an advisory board.</narrative>
  </description>
